WEBVTT

00:00:45.546 --> 00:00:48.799
<i>An unknown frontier</i>

00:00:48.799 --> 00:00:52.386
<i>On the map painted by my heart</i>

00:00:52.386 --> 00:00:59.142
<i>When I open the door, the path goes on</i>

00:00:59.142 --> 00:01:05.107
<i>I'm kicking up dust as I</i>
<i>start running to your town</i>

00:01:05.107 --> 00:01:11.822
<i>Along a route where earth and sky meet</i>

00:01:11.822 --> 00:01:15.576
<i>Riding the rushing southern wind</i>

00:01:15.576 --> 00:01:18.495
<i>Slicing through the wind</i>
<i>dyed blue by the sky</i>

00:01:18.495 --> 00:01:25.627
<i>I'm rushing out with my whole heart</i>

00:01:25.627 --> 00:01:29.131
<i>Shooting past the midday moon</i>

00:01:29.131 --> 00:01:32.259
<i>Towards a world different</i>
<i>from what we've known before</i>

00:01:32.259 --> 00:01:36.096
<i>I will keep on running through to the end</i>

00:01:36.096 --> 00:01:37.681
<i>However far</i>

00:01:37.681 --> 00:01:41.602
<i>Just like that wind</i>

00:01:42.769 --> 00:01:46.899
<i>Just like that wind</i>

00:01:57.993 --> 00:01:58.994
Sousuke!

00:02:00.537 --> 00:02:02.289
That hurt, you know.

00:02:02.289 --> 00:02:04.499
Whose car do you think you're taking apart?

00:02:04.499 --> 00:02:05.501
Unknown.

00:02:05.501 --> 00:02:08.295
That is the precise reason why I'm
investigating this suspicious vehicle.

00:02:08.295 --> 00:02:09.922
Suspicious vehicle?

00:02:09.922 --> 00:02:11.173
A car bomb.

00:02:11.173 --> 00:02:13.133
When loaded with
hidden plastic explosives,

00:02:13.133 --> 00:02:15.469
a vehicle can be turned
into a frightening weapon.

00:02:15.469 --> 00:02:17.137
In 1983, in the Middle East,

00:02:17.137 --> 00:02:20.015
terrorists used a truck to carry out a
kamikaze attack on a US Marine base...

00:02:21.225 --> 00:02:23.310
That one really hurt.

00:02:23.310 --> 00:02:26.104
This is Ms. Kagurazaka's new car!

00:02:26.104 --> 00:02:29.191
I just saw her all happy,
getting ready to wash it!

00:02:29.191 --> 00:02:30.943
That's a problem. I won't be able
to reassemble it very quickly.

00:02:30.943 --> 00:02:32.903
Then don't take it apart
in the first place!

00:02:37.366 --> 00:02:39.159
This is Uruz 7.

00:02:39.159 --> 00:02:40.994
Right.

00:02:40.994 --> 00:02:43.038
2 and 6?

00:02:43.038 --> 00:02:46.708
Understood. I will head to
the site via route 10.

00:02:46.708 --> 00:02:48.460
Something important has come up.
I'm leaving early.

00:02:48.460 --> 00:02:49.962
Again?

00:02:49.962 --> 00:02:51.964
But what are you going to
do about cleaning this up?

00:02:51.964 --> 00:02:53.966
And we have midterm
tests starting tomorrow.

00:02:53.966 --> 00:02:56.510
You know that, right?
Hey, wait, Sousuke!

00:02:56.510 --> 00:02:58.512
Avoid walking outside
alone if at all possible.

00:02:59.721 --> 00:03:01.390
He's gone...

00:03:08.188 --> 00:03:11.733
"Merida Island"
For those reasons, the tracking and monitoring

00:03:11.733 --> 00:03:13.735
"Special Conference Room"
of every individual squad member's past, character,

00:03:13.735 --> 00:03:15.445
"Special Conference Room"
and financial situation is physically impossible.

00:03:15.737 --> 00:03:18.198
Regarding Vincent Bruno's act of treachery,

00:03:18.198 --> 00:03:20.534
"Beautiful Sicily"
considering the fact that he was

00:03:20.534 --> 00:03:21.743
"Beautiful Sicily"
assigned to us in the Intelligence Division,

00:03:21.743 --> 00:03:25.622
we do not deny that we were responsible.

00:03:25.622 --> 00:03:27.332
However, please understand

00:03:27.332 --> 00:03:30.502
that there is a limit to how much
even the Intelligence Division can do.

00:03:31.587 --> 00:03:36.133
After spending 30 minutes reviewing
the report, that's your conclusion?

00:03:36.133 --> 00:03:38.051
That joke isn't funny.

00:03:38.051 --> 00:03:39.261
General Amit,

00:03:39.261 --> 00:03:42.598
isn't there anything you'd like to
add as head of Intelligence?

00:03:42.598 --> 00:03:44.725
This is a structural problem.

00:03:44.725 --> 00:03:48.729
As long as Mithril is a mercenary squad,
no matter how much we pay our personnel,

00:03:48.729 --> 00:03:52.941
there will always be those who
will betray us for even more money.

00:03:52.941 --> 00:03:55.611
I'm sure you haven't
forgotten the past incident

00:03:55.611 --> 00:03:59.072
when terrorists were
allowed to infiltrate the TDD-1.

00:03:59.072 --> 00:04:04.119
A capable commanding officer should notice
if a subordinate is behaving oddly.

00:04:04.119 --> 00:04:06.538
I think this is the responsibility of the
personnel in charge of the scene.

00:04:06.538 --> 00:04:09.583
Isn't running a check on squad members
the job of Intelligence?

00:04:09.583 --> 00:04:13.545
It is irrelevant for you to comment on
the ability of the commanding officer.

00:04:13.545 --> 00:04:15.631
Even if they are clean at the hiring stage,

00:04:15.631 --> 00:04:19.051
we cannot be responsible for them
after they are assigned, Admiral Voda.

00:04:19.051 --> 00:04:22.846
We have a lot of other work
to take care of.

00:04:22.846 --> 00:04:25.807
For example, there is Kaname Chidori,

00:04:25.807 --> 00:04:27.643
whose custody has been
entrusted to the Tactical Division.

00:04:27.643 --> 00:04:30.479
If you would just stop
your "wait and see" attitude,

00:04:30.479 --> 00:04:33.148
and simply hand custody of her
over to the Intelligence Division

00:04:33.148 --> 00:04:36.485
it would save us a
considerable amount of labor.

00:04:36.485 --> 00:04:41.490
I think that the handling of Kaname Chidori
requires the greatest consideration.

00:04:41.490 --> 00:04:43.617
Since you are the same as her,

00:04:43.617 --> 00:04:46.036
that explains why you're extremely
cautious about handling the Whispered,

00:04:46.036 --> 00:04:47.663
correct, Captain Testarossa?

00:04:51.375 --> 00:04:53.585
It seems the discussion
has come to an end.

00:04:53.585 --> 00:04:58.340
Lord Mallory, could we please
have your opinion?

00:04:58.340 --> 00:05:00.676
The structural problem
which Mr. Amit pointed out

00:05:00.676 --> 00:05:03.679
had been anticipated since the
very beginning of Mithril's foundation.

00:05:03.679 --> 00:05:04.847
Unlike a regular military,

00:05:04.847 --> 00:05:09.852
we at Mithril have no cornerstone
such as race, religion, or nation,

00:05:09.852 --> 00:05:13.772
but we must believe in the philosophy of
preventing international disputes,

00:05:13.772 --> 00:05:15.607
which some might have objections to.

00:05:15.607 --> 00:05:18.110
I had thought that all
of you were fighting

00:05:18.110 --> 00:05:20.571
with the full understanding
that these risks were present.

00:05:20.571 --> 00:05:22.364
Was I wrong?

00:05:24.491 --> 00:05:25.409
Very well.

00:05:25.409 --> 00:05:29.663
In that case, let us end the argument
over who is to blame for this problem.

00:05:29.663 --> 00:05:31.874
Of course, we suggest you
consider countermeasures.

00:05:31.874 --> 00:05:36.587
Each of you, reconsider all of the current
procedures and propose countermeasures.

00:05:36.587 --> 00:05:38.797
That is all. Now then, good day.

00:05:45.846 --> 00:05:48.015
It happens every time.

00:05:48.015 --> 00:05:50.893
The Tactical Division demands
more accurate information,

00:05:50.893 --> 00:05:54.104
and the Intelligence Division fires
back that they're doing their best.

00:05:54.104 --> 00:05:56.940
The same kind of thing probably
happens in every kind of organization.

00:05:56.940 --> 00:05:58.609
I know.

00:05:58.609 --> 00:06:00.027
I'm not sure.

00:06:00.027 --> 00:06:04.573
I just don't think your
current position suits you.

00:06:04.573 --> 00:06:06.783
Besides, the Research Division
has important work too.

00:06:06.783 --> 00:06:07.618
Isn't it about time...

00:06:07.618 --> 00:06:11.914
I've said this many times:
I will not leave here!

00:06:14.541 --> 00:06:17.503
You get your stubbornness
from your father.

00:06:17.503 --> 00:06:20.172
He used to give me a hard time too.

00:06:20.172 --> 00:06:25.219
I'm sorry, Uncle. But everyone
here is important to me.

00:06:25.219 --> 00:06:28.055
If only your brother were here,

00:06:28.055 --> 00:06:31.350
that would probably lift half of the
responsibilities off your shoulders.

00:06:31.350 --> 00:06:35.521
I wonder where that Leonard is now,
and what he's doing?

00:06:37.689 --> 00:06:41.693
More importantly,
about that traitor Vincent Bruno.

00:06:41.693 --> 00:06:45.989
It's in progress...
Very far away...

00:06:46.615 --> 00:06:48.116
"Well, Vincent?"

00:06:48.116 --> 00:06:49.785
"Are you doing all right here?"

00:06:49.785 --> 00:06:52.621
"Yes, thank you.
I'm doing very well."

00:06:52.621 --> 00:06:55.791
"You've helped me many times in my work."

00:06:55.791 --> 00:06:57.793
"Now it is my turn to help you."

00:06:57.793 --> 00:07:00.462
"We Sicilians never forget."

00:07:00.462 --> 00:07:01.964
"I trust you."

00:07:01.964 --> 00:07:08.220
"If Amalgam catches me, they will kill me.
If Mithril finds me, they will arrest me."

00:07:08.220 --> 00:07:09.638
"Don't worry."

00:07:09.638 --> 00:07:11.473
"There's a party at my house tonight;"

00:07:11.473 --> 00:07:13.016
"trustworthy people are coming."

00:07:13.016 --> 00:07:15.352
"Relax, and enjoy yourself."

00:07:18.480 --> 00:07:21.316
"La bella Sicilia."
The beautiful island.

00:07:21.316 --> 00:07:23.026
It's just like heaven.

00:07:23.986 --> 00:07:26.488
So, you seem to go for Asian women.

00:07:26.488 --> 00:07:30.325
Yes.
Especially dark-haired beauties like you.

00:07:30.325 --> 00:07:32.536
You're an American, aren't you?

00:07:32.536 --> 00:07:34.371
So you can tell?

00:07:34.371 --> 00:07:38.625
I lived in Baltimore for two years,
so I could tell right away.

00:07:38.625 --> 00:07:43.338
You seem different from the men here.
More "sophisticated," I guess you could say.

00:07:43.338 --> 00:07:46.466
You have a sweet tongue.
I wonder where you picked it up.

00:07:46.466 --> 00:07:47.926
I've forgotten.

00:07:47.926 --> 00:07:50.762
I've had lots of different
experiences here and there.

00:07:50.762 --> 00:07:52.347
What kinds of experiences?

00:07:52.347 --> 00:07:56.518
Come to think of it,
I never asked you your name.

00:07:56.518 --> 00:07:58.395
--Do you want to know?
--I sure do.

00:07:58.395 --> 00:08:03.025
If I don't know, I won't be able to
call out your name when we're doing it.

00:08:03.025 --> 00:08:04.401
Just my name?

00:08:04.401 --> 00:08:06.028
Don't you want to know anything else?

00:08:06.028 --> 00:08:08.113
I sure do.
Of course I do.

00:08:08.113 --> 00:08:10.866
Every little thing about you.

00:08:10.866 --> 00:08:12.034
I see.

00:08:12.034 --> 00:08:12.951
In that case...

00:08:12.951 --> 00:08:13.952
I'll be sure to...

00:08:13.952 --> 00:08:15.787
teach you good!

00:08:18.874 --> 00:08:20.709
Thanks for everything in Nanking!

00:08:20.709 --> 00:08:22.961
My name is Melissa Mao.

00:08:22.961 --> 00:08:24.338
I am assigned to Mithril's
Tactical Division,

00:08:24.338 --> 00:08:27.257
Tuatha de Danaan landing squad, SRT!

00:08:27.257 --> 00:08:28.675
My rank is Sergeant Major!

00:08:28.675 --> 00:08:31.178
My call sign is Uruz 2!

00:08:31.178 --> 00:08:33.013
And not to mention...

00:08:33.013 --> 00:08:35.849
I'm a woman who's itching
to pull the trigger,

00:08:35.849 --> 00:08:38.644
because her comrades
just got killed because of you!

00:08:57.788 --> 00:09:00.374
Don't do it, Big Sis.

00:09:00.374 --> 00:09:02.292
What a dangerous scene.

00:09:02.292 --> 00:09:04.711
I was feeling pretty uneasy
there behind the curtains.

00:09:04.711 --> 00:09:07.673
I thought all I asked you for was a gun.
What were you peeping for?

00:09:07.673 --> 00:09:09.299
Some welcome that is.

00:09:09.299 --> 00:09:12.970
And here I was trying to be a knight
protecting you from the shadows.

00:09:12.970 --> 00:09:15.389
Well, I can understand how you feel, though.

00:09:15.389 --> 00:09:17.182
But we have to be patient at the moment.

00:09:17.182 --> 00:09:20.060
You actually say some
respectable things once in a while.

00:09:20.060 --> 00:09:24.481
I just pretend to be a joker.
This is the real me.

00:09:25.649 --> 00:09:28.068
Maybe it's because of
the moon here in Sicily.

00:09:28.068 --> 00:09:30.320
It feels like even
a love that's always hidden

00:09:30.320 --> 00:09:33.532
could be revealed before
the goddess of the night.

00:09:33.532 --> 00:09:34.908
Did you know?

00:09:34.908 --> 00:09:38.453
Hecate, the goddess of the night,
is also the goddess of revenge.

00:09:38.453 --> 00:09:42.457
That elegant name fits
you so perfectly tonight.

00:09:45.252 --> 00:09:47.045
Could you please
think about where we are?

00:09:47.045 --> 00:09:49.965
This place is crawling
with scary guys, all around us.

00:09:49.965 --> 00:09:52.342
I guess that's the sad reality.

00:09:52.342 --> 00:09:53.635
Okay, let's get to work.

00:09:53.635 --> 00:09:54.469
Sheesh.

00:10:02.019 --> 00:10:03.353
What about the route to the car?

00:10:03.353 --> 00:10:05.606
No problem.
I knocked them all out.

00:10:14.573 --> 00:10:15.657
It's just past these bushes.

00:10:15.657 --> 00:10:17.159
Okay.

00:10:19.494 --> 00:10:21.788
Hi there.

00:10:26.543 --> 00:10:28.128
What was that about
knocking them all out?

00:10:28.128 --> 00:10:30.506
How am I supposed to know
about something like<i> that</i>?

00:10:32.007 --> 00:10:33.717
Our backs are up against a wall now.

00:10:33.717 --> 00:10:35.427
And on top of that,
this is the only weapon we've got.

00:10:35.427 --> 00:10:37.804
Shit, if I just had a rifle.

00:10:37.804 --> 00:10:40.516
Now that it's come down to this,
we should kill this guy before we die!

00:10:40.516 --> 00:10:41.099
Hey!

00:10:41.099 --> 00:10:42.601
Don't get desperate, Uruz 2.

00:10:42.601 --> 00:10:43.519
Sousuke?

00:10:44.520 --> 00:10:46.605
Escape through the hole I just made.

00:10:49.733 --> 00:10:50.567
Sousuke?

00:10:50.567 --> 00:10:52.069
Don't you have tests today?

00:10:52.069 --> 00:10:53.070
Affirmative.

00:10:53.070 --> 00:10:55.322
However, the escape route has changed.

00:10:55.322 --> 00:10:56.740
I came to deliver that message,
and provide back-up.

00:10:56.740 --> 00:10:57.741
Changed?

00:10:57.741 --> 00:10:59.159
The helicopter will...

00:10:59.159 --> 00:11:00.118
Explain later!

00:11:00.118 --> 00:11:01.119
Roger.

00:11:04.289 --> 00:11:06.458
The helicopter will pick us up directly.

00:11:06.458 --> 00:11:08.877
I'll lead you to the rendezvous point.

00:11:08.877 --> 00:11:10.420
Incidentally, that's a strange
bathing suit you have on.

00:11:10.420 --> 00:11:12.089
Wrong! This is for social use!

00:11:12.089 --> 00:11:13.507
They're here!

00:11:15.092 --> 00:11:17.719
5, 6, 7, 8, 9...

00:11:17.719 --> 00:11:19.263
Thirteen cars?

00:11:19.263 --> 00:11:20.889
Can't this thing go any faster?

00:11:20.889 --> 00:11:24.560
Impossible. I'm afraid it's an old car,
so it doesn't have much power.

00:11:24.560 --> 00:11:25.477
Dammit!

00:11:25.477 --> 00:11:26.937
They're gonna shoot!
Get down!

00:11:29.690 --> 00:11:31.149
Shit!

00:11:31.149 --> 00:11:33.777
Damn, they're bulletproof.
Figures.

00:11:35.904 --> 00:11:37.990
Maybe we should kill him
and dump him after all.

00:11:37.990 --> 00:11:40.826
Yeah, I'm beginning to
think that's a good idea, too.

00:11:40.826 --> 00:11:42.035
Are we lightening the car?

00:11:42.035 --> 00:11:44.329
That's right. If we don't,
they're going to catch up with us.

00:11:44.329 --> 00:11:46.957
In that case, just that man
won't be enough.

00:11:46.957 --> 00:11:50.502
There are weapons in the back seat,
so throw those away, too.

00:11:50.502 --> 00:11:51.837
Weapons?!

00:11:54.423 --> 00:11:56.133
You should've told us sooner, idiot!

00:11:56.133 --> 00:11:57.176
I didn't tell you?

00:11:57.176 --> 00:11:59.469
No, you didn't. Jeez...

00:12:09.229 --> 00:12:11.398
What's going on?
What's all the noise--?

00:12:11.398 --> 00:12:12.566
You seem happy.

00:12:12.566 --> 00:12:14.109
It's just your imagination.

00:12:17.613 --> 00:12:20.073
All right, let's continue the party!

00:12:20.073 --> 00:12:21.992
You guys ready?

00:12:21.992 --> 00:12:23.535
--Any time.
--Anywhere!

00:12:24.620 --> 00:12:27.122
<i>Rock and roll</i>!

00:12:42.429 --> 00:12:44.473
This has turned into one hell of a parade!

00:12:44.473 --> 00:12:47.100
This must be disturbing the good citizens.

00:12:47.100 --> 00:12:48.227
Kurz, cover me!

00:12:48.227 --> 00:12:49.269
Sure thing!

00:12:57.778 --> 00:12:59.613
I wonder which one of us
is the disturbance?

00:12:59.613 --> 00:13:00.656
We're turning!

00:13:02.241 --> 00:13:04.243
You should've said
that sooner, you idiot!

00:13:15.003 --> 00:13:16.922
Like I said,
tell me soon--

00:13:16.922 --> 00:13:18.841
Don't look!

00:13:18.841 --> 00:13:20.300
That hurt!

00:13:20.300 --> 00:13:21.844
Next time you face front,
I'll kill you!

00:13:21.844 --> 00:13:23.220
Okay, okay!

00:13:24.096 --> 00:13:25.264
We're getting out of the village!

00:13:26.014 --> 00:13:29.643
All right!
I'm gonna give 'em one big shot!

00:13:41.780 --> 00:13:43.365
Our plans have been upset.

00:13:43.365 --> 00:13:44.908
What are your orders, Mr. Gates?

00:13:44.908 --> 00:13:46.827
This is perfect!

00:13:46.827 --> 00:13:50.330
They saved us the
trouble of bringing him out.

00:13:50.330 --> 00:13:54.751
Show our thanks by silencing all of them.

00:13:54.751 --> 00:13:55.919
Roger.

00:13:58.213 --> 00:14:01.842
Yeah. I can't tonight,
I'm in the middle of tests.

00:14:01.842 --> 00:14:05.888
Yeah. Yeah.
Yeah, I'm doing my best.

00:14:05.888 --> 00:14:08.348
Umm, so-so, I guess.

00:14:08.348 --> 00:14:11.059
Hey, when can I see you again?

00:14:11.059 --> 00:14:11.727
Yeah.

00:14:11.727 --> 00:14:12.686
Dammit.

00:14:12.686 --> 00:14:14.354
--Hey, Kana-<i>chan</i>!
--What, really? Yeah, I want to go.

00:14:14.354 --> 00:14:16.648
--Did you study for the tests?
--What, really? Yeah, I want to go.

00:14:16.648 --> 00:14:18.692
Umm, kind of. What about you?

00:14:18.692 --> 00:14:20.360
Not at all.

00:14:21.403 --> 00:14:24.072
Not that I'm in a position to be
worried about others, but...

00:14:24.072 --> 00:14:26.617
I noticed Sagara
didn't come again today.

00:14:26.617 --> 00:14:28.660
Will he be all right
not taking the tests?

00:14:28.660 --> 00:14:31.705
Really. I wonder if that
idiot doesn't mind failing his classes.

00:14:31.705 --> 00:14:33.707
Have you tried calling
him on his cell phone?

00:14:33.707 --> 00:14:36.793
He might actually come
if you pressure him.

00:14:36.793 --> 00:14:37.920
What are you talking about?

00:14:37.920 --> 00:14:39.588
No use even bothering.

00:14:39.588 --> 00:14:42.382
I can never get in touch
with him at times like this.

00:14:42.382 --> 00:14:45.135
I don't know where he is
or what he's doing.

00:14:45.135 --> 00:14:47.596
I can't even reach his voice mail.

00:14:47.596 --> 00:14:50.057
It's<i> such </i>a pain. He should try
putting himself in my shoes.

00:14:50.057 --> 00:14:52.226
I'm over here trying
to contact him all the time.

00:14:52.226 --> 00:14:53.101
I got through.

00:14:53.101 --> 00:14:54.269
Huh?

00:14:57.105 --> 00:14:58.732
Really?

00:15:00.692 --> 00:15:01.944
And then...

00:15:05.781 --> 00:15:07.866
Hello, Sousuke?

00:15:07.866 --> 00:15:09.034
Chidori? What's wrong?

00:15:09.034 --> 00:15:11.870
The static is horrible.
Where are you?

00:15:11.870 --> 00:15:13.539
Canicattì.

00:15:13.539 --> 00:15:16.416
Can cutting... What?

00:15:17.167 --> 00:15:20.170
Listen, the tests have
already started, you know!

00:15:20.170 --> 00:15:21.672
Did you forget?

00:15:21.672 --> 00:15:24.716
I remember, but something important came up.
It was unavoidable.

00:15:24.716 --> 00:15:29.263
Don't give me that excuse.
I even lent you my Classics notes.

00:15:29.263 --> 00:15:31.390
And then there's that thing
about Ms. Kagurazaka's car.

00:15:31.390 --> 00:15:33.767
I had a really hard time
calming her down, you know.

00:15:33.767 --> 00:15:35.727
I'm sorry about that.

00:15:35.727 --> 00:15:38.105
"Sorry" isn't going to cut it.

00:15:38.105 --> 00:15:40.107
Do you have any idea how
mentally drained you make me feel?

00:15:40.107 --> 00:15:41.149
I understand.

00:15:41.149 --> 00:15:43.485
No you don't!
You don't mean that at all!

00:15:43.485 --> 00:15:44.736
Hey, are you listening to me?

00:15:44.736 --> 00:15:46.864
Yeah, I'm listening!
I'm listening!

00:15:46.864 --> 00:15:48.156
I'm going straight through!

00:15:48.156 --> 00:15:49.032
Wh-What?

00:15:49.032 --> 00:15:50.242
Nothing, just something on my end.

00:15:50.242 --> 00:15:51.493
I'm driving right now.

00:15:54.371 --> 00:15:55.289
Four more!

00:15:55.289 --> 00:15:57.916
Hello? Did you say
you're driving? A car?

00:15:57.916 --> 00:15:58.834
Affirmative.

00:15:58.834 --> 00:16:00.043
That's dangerous.

00:16:00.043 --> 00:16:02.921
It's against traffic laws to
use a cell phone while driving.

00:16:02.921 --> 00:16:04.756
And in the first place,
you're only a high school student!

00:16:04.756 --> 00:16:07.134
Just stop the car somewhere.

00:16:07.134 --> 00:16:08.343
I can't do that.

00:16:08.343 --> 00:16:09.970
If I stop I won't be able to
take the make-up tests either!

00:16:09.970 --> 00:16:11.013
Huh?

00:16:11.013 --> 00:16:13.182
Oh yeah, that pretty woman...

00:16:13.182 --> 00:16:16.018
Listen, your grades are in serious danger.

00:16:16.018 --> 00:16:17.853
And you're always out of school.

00:16:17.853 --> 00:16:19.062
I have a mission.
I have no choice.

00:16:19.062 --> 00:16:21.857
But you can't explain
that to the teacher, you know?

00:16:21.857 --> 00:16:24.193
If you fail, you won't be able
to move on to the next grade!

00:16:24.193 --> 00:16:25.819
Now that you mention it,
you're right!

00:16:25.819 --> 00:16:27.821
What'll you do if you
have to repeat a grade?

00:16:27.821 --> 00:16:30.407
We'll end up
graduating before you!

00:16:30.407 --> 00:16:32.075
That would be a problem!

00:16:32.075 --> 00:16:33.535
It would be a problem for me too.

00:16:33.535 --> 00:16:34.953
What did you say?

00:16:34.953 --> 00:16:36.330
Nothing.

00:16:36.330 --> 00:16:37.873
I couldn't hear you!
Please repeat!

00:16:37.873 --> 00:16:38.832
One more left!

00:16:38.832 --> 00:16:40.876
No! A woman's panties should be white--!

00:16:40.876 --> 00:16:42.836
What? Is someone there?

00:16:42.836 --> 00:16:44.796
Don't worry about it!
Now what was it you were just saying?

00:16:44.796 --> 00:16:47.508
Just forget it.
You're in your own world anyway.

00:16:47.508 --> 00:16:49.927
No, the surroundings are...

00:16:49.927 --> 00:16:51.094
are noisy.

00:16:51.094 --> 00:16:53.472
You know, Sousuke...

00:16:53.472 --> 00:16:57.684
Sometimes I get the feeling that
you never listen to me seriously.

00:16:57.684 --> 00:16:59.311
That's a misunderstanding, Chidori!

00:16:59.311 --> 00:17:00.062
I don't know about that...

00:17:00.062 --> 00:17:01.104
It's true!

00:17:01.104 --> 00:17:03.440
I swear!
I'm always serious!

00:17:03.440 --> 00:17:04.942
--I'm talking to you right now...
--Get down!

00:17:04.942 --> 00:17:05.442
Huh?

00:17:06.485 --> 00:17:07.569
Who was that?

00:17:07.569 --> 00:17:10.822
Hey, come on! Hello? Hello?

00:17:12.824 --> 00:17:14.701
XO! Immediately...

00:17:14.701 --> 00:17:16.703
Chidori, everything is
under control now.

00:17:16.703 --> 00:17:18.872
What was it you wanted to talk about?

00:17:18.872 --> 00:17:19.915
Just forget it.

00:17:19.915 --> 00:17:20.832
Chidori?

00:17:20.832 --> 00:17:23.919
Anyway, get back to
school as soon as you can.

00:17:23.919 --> 00:17:25.254
--Yeah, I...
--Idiot.

00:17:26.421 --> 00:17:29.091
What's wrong, Sousuke?

00:17:29.091 --> 00:17:30.551
AS at 8:00!

00:17:30.551 --> 00:17:31.885
This isn't good.

00:17:31.885 --> 00:17:33.011
I'm not doing so good either.

00:17:33.011 --> 00:17:34.137
Floor it, Sousuke!

00:17:34.137 --> 00:17:35.430
I know!

00:17:37.266 --> 00:17:38.392
Savages?

00:17:38.392 --> 00:17:40.727
Even the Mafia has
those things these days?

00:17:40.727 --> 00:17:42.271
I never heard anything about that!

00:17:42.271 --> 00:17:43.605
Then what are those, illusions?!

00:17:43.605 --> 00:17:45.023
Why don't you ask<i> them</i>!

00:17:45.023 --> 00:17:48.902
Come on, Sousuke, speed it up!
Those things can run over 100 kph!

00:17:48.902 --> 00:17:52.281
I'm already making her go as fast
as she can. This is all she's got.

00:17:52.281 --> 00:17:53.448
They're gonna shoot!

00:18:07.004 --> 00:18:08.297
The engine!

00:18:14.928 --> 00:18:15.971
What?

00:18:28.317 --> 00:18:29.401
An M9?

00:18:29.401 --> 00:18:30.986
That's one of ours, right?

00:18:30.986 --> 00:18:32.112
Where's he assigned?

00:18:32.112 --> 00:18:33.447
Don't know.

00:18:52.966 --> 00:18:55.052
Looks like they came to get us.

00:18:55.052 --> 00:18:56.970
You failed?!

00:18:56.970 --> 00:18:58.680
Yes, sir.
Three Savages were destroyed.

00:18:59.681 --> 00:19:01.517
But all operators were killed,

00:19:01.517 --> 00:19:05.270
so you do not... have to worry...
about information about us... leaking out!

00:19:08.273 --> 00:19:11.610
With Bruno taken away from us,
that doesn't mean a thing!

00:19:11.610 --> 00:19:14.404
The stealing of the Arbalest!
Finishing off Bruno!

00:19:14.404 --> 00:19:18.158
You failed your mission twice in a row!

00:19:24.998 --> 00:19:28.418
Actually, I can't afford
to keep failing anymore.

00:19:28.418 --> 00:19:31.296
I need to score some points somewhere.

00:19:31.296 --> 00:19:34.258
It seems like it's time
for us to say goodbye.

00:19:34.258 --> 00:19:35.634
After taking<i> that</i>?

00:19:35.634 --> 00:19:38.637
Yes, after taking<i> that</i>.

00:19:40.305 --> 00:19:44.977
You can tell us, can't you?
Who in the world was in that black M9?

00:19:44.977 --> 00:19:46.603
None of you are authorized to know.

00:19:46.603 --> 00:19:48.647
Not even me, the commanding
officer in the field?

00:19:48.647 --> 00:19:49.982
You will find out soon enough.

00:19:49.982 --> 00:19:53.402
Once you return to base,
hurry up with the report. That is all.

00:19:53.402 --> 00:19:56.071
This pisses me off, dammit!

00:19:56.071 --> 00:20:00.450
Why is that old geezer always,
always, always like that?

00:20:00.450 --> 00:20:02.536
Couldn't agree more. Right, Sousuke?

00:20:05.497 --> 00:20:07.249
Studying for midterms?

00:20:07.249 --> 00:20:08.458
Affirmative.

00:20:08.458 --> 00:20:10.669
I can't afford to fail any more classes.

00:20:10.669 --> 00:20:12.254
If your grades are that bad,

00:20:12.254 --> 00:20:14.631
don't you think you should've
stayed in Japan and studied?

00:20:14.631 --> 00:20:16.508
Kaname's worried too, right?

00:20:16.508 --> 00:20:18.427
This work is important, too.

00:20:18.427 --> 00:20:21.180
What would've happened if I hadn't come?

00:20:21.180 --> 00:20:22.598
We would've been able to handle it somehow.

00:20:22.598 --> 00:20:24.516
Right, Big Sis?

00:20:24.516 --> 00:20:28.103
Well, to be honest,
I did have some backup plans.

00:20:29.605 --> 00:20:30.731
I see...

00:20:31.940 --> 00:20:34.359
Ah, but it is true that you saved us.

00:20:34.359 --> 00:20:37.321
But you know, I am a little worried.
In other words...

00:20:37.321 --> 00:20:38.363
About if I'll be able to
move to the next grade?

00:20:38.363 --> 00:20:42.117
No, about your entire situation right now.

00:20:42.117 --> 00:20:45.454
You're guarding Kaname,
participating in missions like this,

00:20:45.454 --> 00:20:47.539
and operating the Arbalest on top of that.

00:20:47.539 --> 00:20:49.499
Isn't that too much of a burden for you?

00:20:49.499 --> 00:20:53.670
At first, I thought you'd be okay
if it was just for a short time,

00:20:53.670 --> 00:20:57.508
because you handled the work
without any problems. But lately...

00:20:57.508 --> 00:20:59.176
I haven't made any mistakes.

00:20:59.176 --> 00:21:00.260
No, not yet.

00:21:00.260 --> 00:21:03.555
But there's a limit to how much you can do,
no matter how short on personnel we are.

00:21:03.555 --> 00:21:08.101
There's no reason why you have to
be the only one guarding Kaname.

00:21:12.147 --> 00:21:14.358
What do<i> you </i>think?

00:21:14.358 --> 00:21:15.400
About what?

00:21:15.400 --> 00:21:18.487
Your plans for the future!

00:21:18.487 --> 00:21:21.698
Follow orders. That's all.

00:21:21.698 --> 00:21:23.450
You're always like that!

00:21:23.450 --> 00:21:27.079
I'm talking about your plans
for your life, your<i> future!</i>

00:21:27.079 --> 00:21:28.747
You're still just 17 years old, you know?

00:21:28.747 --> 00:21:32.167
Don't you ever think just
a little bit about the future?

00:21:32.167 --> 00:21:34.086
Aren't you running away from everything

00:21:34.086 --> 00:21:35.671
using your "mission" and
"orders" as an excuse?

00:21:35.671 --> 00:21:37.130
Running away?<i> Me</i>?

00:21:37.130 --> 00:21:38.215
That's right!

00:21:38.215 --> 00:21:42.386
Life must be a lot easier when all you
do is follow what other people say, huh?

00:21:44.847 --> 00:21:47.182
What's up with you getting into
his business like that, Big Sis?

00:21:47.182 --> 00:21:50.018
I'm not. It's just something
I've been thinking about for a while.

00:21:50.018 --> 00:21:53.647
Well, don't strain
yourself with your studies.

00:21:53.647 --> 00:21:56.108
You got into the school
using fake documents anyway,

00:21:56.108 --> 00:21:59.111
so there's no reason
you have to graduate, you know?

00:22:11.832 --> 00:22:13.250
The future...

00:22:27.764 --> 00:22:29.516
<i>I'm sure you're still looking</i>

00:22:29.516 --> 00:22:33.312
<i>Straight ahead to tomorrow</i>

00:22:33.312 --> 00:22:39.193
<i>Just like you always have</i>

00:22:39.193 --> 00:22:44.907
<i>Just like the sunflowers</i>

00:22:44.907 --> 00:22:51.663
<i>That bloomed on that windy hill</i>

00:22:53.582 --> 00:22:59.505
<i>No matter how far apart we are</i>

00:22:59.505 --> 00:23:05.511
<i>I pray that my singing will reach you</i>

00:23:05.511 --> 00:23:11.558
<i>On nights when the tears never seem to stop</i>

00:23:11.558 --> 00:23:14.895
<i>I want to be the moon</i>

00:23:14.895 --> 00:23:17.898
<i>That shines through your window</i>

00:23:17.898 --> 00:23:25.948
<i>Because I believe we will meet again</i>

00:23:28.283 --> 00:23:31.870
<i>No matter what</i>

00:23:45.175 --> 00:23:46.718
"Next Episode"

00:23:46.718 --> 00:23:49.221
<i>Quiet times have returned.</i>

00:23:49.221 --> 00:23:52.474
<i>The days go by. The seasons change.</i>

00:23:52.474 --> 00:23:54.977
<i>Drenched in a peace</i>
<i>I had never known before,</i>

00:23:54.977 --> 00:23:58.313
<i>I dozed off in the silence.</i>

00:23:58.313 --> 00:24:00.816
<i>Next time: "Edge of Heaven."</i>

00:24:00.816 --> 00:24:04.672
<i>Dark clouds gather near without a sound.</i>
